Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket and its own fix.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} {issues} />

## What each problem is

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get day and
  month swapped. This is what #4471 describes.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then reads the date
  day first. People type what the hint says. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants.

A few `parser` reports describe a one-day move, not a swap (the desk's `oneDayMove` notes). The
desk counts them under `parser` by tenant; the table footnotes them.

## How the count works

- One report per id: the export repeats some rows.
- Cause by tenant and channel (`causes.ts`), never by `meta.intakeTag`, which is a browser guess.
- The table is computed at render time, so it follows the data as the desk keeps working.

